Enable on the libretro device the features the renderer assumes it has

In a libretro build the core makes its Vulkan device itself, through the
negotiation interface (LibRetro::CreateVulkanDevice). The renderer's Instance
then reads the features from the GPU (Instance::CreateDevice, FEAT_SET) and
returns before making a device of its own (HAVE_LIBRETRO). So it records as
present every feature the GPU OFFERS, whether or not the device it uses enabled
it. Three of those were never enabled by CreateVulkanDevice:

- VK_EXT_pipeline_creation_cache_control (pipelineCreationCacheControl)
- VK_EXT_robustness2 (nullDescriptor)
- VK_EXT_fragment_shader_interlock (fragmentShaderPixelInterlock)

The first one is felt. GraphicsPipeline::TryBuild, on the emulation thread,
asks the driver for each new pipeline with
FAIL_ON_PIPELINE_COMPILE_REQUIRED, expecting a refusal when the driver would
have to compile, and then hands the compile to its worker threads, while the
draws that need the pipeline are skipped (async shader compilation). A driver
honours that flag only when the feature is enabled on the device (MoltenVK:
MVKPipeline::shouldFailOnPipelineCompileRequired). On MoltenVK it was not, so
the "quick" try compiled the whole pipeline (SPIR-V to MSL to Metal) right
there.

On an iPhone 14 Pro (Majora's Mask 3D, async shader compilation on,
2026-10-19), the game ran at 60 fps with 6 ms of work per frame, and stopped
for 0.4 to 2.9 seconds at a new scene. Every stop came right after MoltenVK's
"Compilation succeeded" line, on the emulation thread.

This patch enables the three extensions and their features on the device,
each only where the GPU reports the feature: the same reading the Instance
already makes. The renderer's code is unchanged; what it already relied on is
now true of its device.

The stall itself cannot be measured on the host bench: lavapipe compiles a
pipeline in well under a frame. Nor is the host output deterministic run to
run, even with async compilation off: Tools/3ds-bench hash over 1800 frames of
Majora's Mask 3D, five cold runs each, differs in 0 to 4 frames between runs of
the SAME build, and the builds with and without this patch fall in that same
spread. Bench frame times are unchanged. On the phone (2026-10-19) the device
now lists the three extensions, and the longest stop at a new scene went from
2.9 to 1.1 seconds; patch 0006 is what removes the rest.

diff --git a/src/citra_libretro/libretro_vk.cpp b/src/citra_libretro/libretro_vk.cpp
index 0a4c66e..9588ab9 100644
--- a/src/citra_libretro/libretro_vk.cpp
+++ b/src/citra_libretro/libretro_vk.cpp
@@ -101,6 +101,23 @@ bool CreateVulkanDevice(struct retro_vulkan_context* context, VkInstance instanc
     const bool has_custom_border_color = AddExtensionIfAvailable(
         enabled_exts, available_exts, VK_EXT_CUSTOM_BORDER_COLOR_EXTENSION_NAME);
 
+    // Instance::CreateDevice decides these three from what the GPU OFFERS and,
+    // in a libretro build, returns before creating a device: this one is the
+    // device it uses, so it enables them, or the renderer relies on features
+    // its device does not have. Pipeline creation cache control is the one
+    // that is felt: GraphicsPipeline::TryBuild asks the driver for a pipeline
+    // with FAIL_ON_PIPELINE_COMPILE_REQUIRED on the emulation thread, expecting
+    // a refusal when it would have to compile, and hands the compile to its
+    // workers. A driver honours that flag only when the feature is enabled
+    // (MoltenVK: MVKPipeline::shouldFailOnPipelineCompileRequired), so without
+    // it every new pipeline was compiled right there, and the game stopped.
+    const bool has_pipeline_creation_cache_control = AddExtensionIfAvailable(
+        enabled_exts, available_exts, VK_EXT_PIPELINE_CREATION_CACHE_CONTROL_EXTENSION_NAME);
+    const bool has_robustness2 =
+        AddExtensionIfAvailable(enabled_exts, available_exts, VK_EXT_ROBUSTNESS_2_EXTENSION_NAME);
+    const bool has_fragment_shader_interlock = AddExtensionIfAvailable(
+        enabled_exts, available_exts, VK_EXT_FRAGMENT_SHADER_INTERLOCK_EXTENSION_NAME);
+
     // These are beneficial but blacklisted on some platforms due to driver bugs
     // For now, let the Instance class handle these decisions
     // AddExtensionIfAvailable(enabled_exts, available_exts,
@@ -180,6 +197,49 @@ bool CreateVulkanDevice(struct retro_vulkan_context* context, VkInstance instanc
         enabled_features.pNext = &custom_border_color_features;
     }
 
+    // The three features above, each enabled only where the GPU reports it,
+    // the same reading Instance::CreateDevice makes (FEAT_SET).
+    VkPhysicalDevicePipelineCreationCacheControlFeaturesEXT supported_pcc{
+        VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_PIPELINE_CREATION_CACHE_CONTROL_FEATURES_EXT};
+    VkPhysicalDeviceRobustness2FeaturesEXT supported_robustness2{
+        VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_ROBUSTNESS_2_FEATURES_EXT};
+    VkPhysicalDeviceFragmentShaderInterlockFeaturesEXT supported_interlock{
+        VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_FRAGMENT_SHADER_INTERLOCK_FEATURES_EXT};
+    supported_pcc.pNext = &supported_robustness2;
+    supported_robustness2.pNext = &supported_interlock;
+    VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 supported{VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_FEATURES_2};
+    supported.pNext = &supported_pcc;
+    PFN_vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 =
+        (PFN_vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2)get_instance_proc_addr(instance,
+                                                                 "vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2");
+    if (vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2) {
+        vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2(gpu, &supported);
+    }
+
+    VkPhysicalDevicePipelineCreationCacheControlFeaturesEXT pcc_features{
+        VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_PIPELINE_CREATION_CACHE_CONTROL_FEATURES_EXT};
+    if (has_pipeline_creation_cache_control && supported_pcc.pipelineCreationCacheControl) {
+        pcc_features.pipelineCreationCacheControl = VK_TRUE;
+        pcc_features.pNext = enabled_features.pNext;
+        enabled_features.pNext = &pcc_features;
+    }
+
+    VkPhysicalDeviceRobustness2FeaturesEXT robustness2_features{
+        VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_ROBUSTNESS_2_FEATURES_EXT};
+    if (has_robustness2 && supported_robustness2.nullDescriptor) {
+        robustness2_features.nullDescriptor = VK_TRUE;
+        robustness2_features.pNext = enabled_features.pNext;
+        enabled_features.pNext = &robustness2_features;
+    }
+
+    VkPhysicalDeviceFragmentShaderInterlockFeaturesEXT interlock_features{
+        VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_FRAGMENT_SHADER_INTERLOCK_FEATURES_EXT};
+    if (has_fragment_shader_interlock && supported_interlock.fragmentShaderPixelInterlock) {
+        interlock_features.fragmentShaderPixelInterlock = VK_TRUE;
+        interlock_features.pNext = enabled_features.pNext;
+        enabled_features.pNext = &interlock_features;
+    }
+
     VkDeviceCreateInfo device_info{VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_DEVICE_CREATE_INFO};
     device_info.queueCreateInfoCount = 1;
     device_info.pQueueCreateInfos = &queue_info;
